WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.933
If you had to walk on hot sand with a heavy backpack and no water to drink, how long could you walk?

2
00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:13.138
Could you walk for ten minutes? Could you walk for one hour?

3
00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:20.902
Could you walk for three weeks? There is one animal that can: the camel!

4
00:00:20.903 --> 00:00:25.334
There are two kinds of camels, the Dromedary and the Bactrian.

5
00:00:25.335 --> 00:00:30.314
Dromedary camels have only one hump and Bactrian camels have two.

6
00:00:30.315 --> 00:00:37.560
If you turn the letters D and B on their sides, this will help you remember their names.

7
00:00:37.561 --> 00:00:42.061
Dromedary camels live in Arabia, India, and North Africa.

8
00:00:42.062 --> 00:00:49.400
There are 13 million Dromedary camels alive today, and all of them are used to carry loads through the desert.

9
00:00:49.401 --> 00:00:56.707
Because they are so valuable to humans, there are no more wild Dromedary camels.

10
00:00:56.708 --> 00:01:01.329
Bactrian camels live in China, Mongolia, and Kazakhstan.

11
00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:06.693
Scientists are worried because there are not many wild Bactrian camels left in the world.

12
00:01:06.694 --> 00:01:11.107
There are only 950 living in the Gobi Desert.

13
00:01:11.108 --> 00:01:19.026
Bactrian camels are slower than Dromedary camels, so people prefer Dromedaries.

14
00:01:19.027 --> 00:01:23.675
Do you wish you had a camel? If you do, listen to this.

15
00:01:23.676 --> 00:01:25.983
Camels are very difficult pets.

16
00:01:25.984 --> 00:01:30.213
They like to bite, spit, and kick people who make them work.

17
00:01:30.214 --> 00:01:38.080
Camels eat 12 kilograms of food every day and can drink 114 liters of water in ten minutes!

18
00:01:38.081 --> 00:01:41.430
But there are a lot of good things about camels too.

19
00:01:41.431 --> 00:01:47.017
Camel milk is very delicious. And camel wool can be made into clothes.

20
00:01:47.018 --> 00:01:51.655
If you need to light a fire, you can use camel dung.

21
00:01:51.656 --> 00:01:56.749
These three camel gifts help people survive in the desert.

22
00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.125
But wait, there is more!

23
00:01:59.126 --> 00:02:06.338
Camels are called ships of the desert because they carry very big loads from one side of the desert to the other.

24
00:02:06.339 --> 00:02:12.581
Dromedary camels can carry over two hundred kilograms on their backs.

25
00:02:12.582 --> 00:02:16.784
Camels walk four kilometers per hour through the hot desert.

26
00:02:16.785 --> 00:02:21.951
They can go like this for three weeks without water! That's amazing!

27
00:02:21.952 --> 00:02:24.834
Why don't camels need water?

28
00:02:24.835 --> 00:02:28.283
Here's a hint: they don't store it in their humps.

29
00:02:28.284 --> 00:02:32.528
Camels do need water, but they save it for long trips.

30
00:02:32.529 --> 00:02:37.052
For example, when the weather gets hot, camels don't sweat much.

31
00:02:37.053 --> 00:02:41.152
Instead, they let their bodies get warmer.

32
00:02:41.153 --> 00:02:47.201
Even when camels go to the bathroom, they save their water and only lose the waste.

33
00:02:47.202 --> 00:02:52.571
A camel can lose up to 40 percent of its body's water before getting sick.

34
00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:55.725
Humans can lose only 20 percent.

35
00:02:55.726 --> 00:03:01.541
These are just some of the reasons that camels don't need water in the desert.

36
00:03:01.542 --> 00:03:05.714
So what is in the camel's hump? Good question.

37
00:03:05.715 --> 00:03:09.466
When camels are not walking, they eat a lot of food.

38
00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:14.414
Their bodies turn the food into fat and save the fat in their humps.

39
00:03:14.415 --> 00:03:18.742
The fat helps them walk for many weeks without eating.

40
00:03:18.743 --> 00:03:22.825
The next time you see a picture of a camel, look at its hump.

41
00:03:22.826 --> 00:03:26.581
If the hump is tall, it means the camel is healthy.

42
00:03:26.582 --> 00:03:35.856
If the hump is short or falling over, it means the camel needs a vacation and lots to eat and drink!

43
00:03:35.857 --> 00:03:40.732
Camels are amazing animals. They can close their noses in sandstorms.

44
00:03:40.733 --> 00:03:43.900
They can eat thorn bushes without hurting their lips.

45
00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:46.640
They can live to be forty years old.

46
00:03:46.641 --> 00:03:55.450
It's no wonder the Bedouin, the desert people of northern Africa, call camels the gift of God!

